6. MEASUREMENT SOURCE - Sleipner CO2 Reference Dataset  (NO DATA REDISTRIBUTED)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    SDIP's at-scale measurements - the certificate recorded as row 1 of
    EQUIVALENCE_LEDGER.md, and the scale figures in DECISIONS.md and
    OPEN_DEBTS.md - were taken against the Sleipner CO2 Reference Dataset.

        Dataset   Sleipner 4D seismic dataset (2006 vintage, full-stack volume)
        Owner     The Sleipner Group
        Operator  Equinor Energy AS
        Partners  ExxonMobil Exploration and Production Norway AS,
                  LOTOS Exploration and Production Norge AS,
                  KUFPEC Norway AS
        Portal    CO2DataShare - https://co2datashare.org/dataset/
                  sleipner-4d-seismic-dataset
        Licence   Sleipner CO2 Reference Dataset License
                  (the licence document distributed inside the dataset bag)
        Use       Downloaded and used under that licence. Its section 3.1 grants
                  a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive licence to download
                  and use the Licensed Material.

    NO SLEIPNER DATA IS REDISTRIBUTED BY THIS PROJECT, IN ANY FORM, AT ANY SIZE.
    The dataset is not in this repository, not in its history, not in the
    published wheel, sdist or container image, and is not fetched by any test.
    What appears in the public record is measurements ABOUT the data - SHA-256
    digests, byte counts, trace counts, timings - and a digest is not data
    (D-0025). The certificate JSON itself stays in the firewalled tree.

    Attribution is given here because section 3.3 of that licence conditions
    sharing on attributing The Sleipner Group and including a notice referring
    to its terms. SDIP shares measurements rather than material, so the
    condition is arguably not triggered at all; it is honoured regardless,
    because naming a dataset publicly while omitting who owns it is the wrong
    default whether or not a clause compels it.

    NO ENDORSEMENT. Section 4 of that licence forbids using The Sleipner Group's
    name, or the names or trademarks of its participating companies, to support,
    recommend or market any product or use. Nothing here does so. The dataset is
    named in this project's engineering records as the factual provenance of a
    measurement, and it must not be used to promote SDIP.

    ON "ADAPTED MATERIAL". Section 2.1 of that licence provides that changes in
    formatting and file types which do not affect the content do not produce
    Adapted Material - the result remains Licensed Material. An SDIP conversion
    is precisely such a change, and the Equivalence Certificate is the evidence
    that it is. The distinction is recorded because it determines which of the
    licence's obligations would attach to a converted store, not because SDIP
    holds one out for distribution. It does not.

